+# Independent corrected U1 dictionary review
+
+Mathematical PASS for corrected DERIVATION.md SHA a70724ba0ae48a66a7e416bbd5c6ee5d1eb5b56024a46c7989a633cd30dc4d51, with exactly its supplied finite six-valent bipartite low-charge carrier, redundant no-double representation and projected operator scope. This is not a physical implementation, continuum or audit verdict.
+
+Root supplied the target and exposed the original absolute hole-basis error before this review. I read the complete corrected proof, complete author check.py and its preregistration, current PR8038 source, and the earlier supplied U1-link source. I did not import or rerun the author checker. My separate implementation reconstructs an actual L4 graph with vertex labels permuted by (13lex+7)mod64 and alternating ascending/descending neighbor orders.
+
+## Absolute basis phase: original issue independently confirmed
+
+For increasing I, product c_i acts rightmost first. Removing larger indices first leaves every lower occupied index unchanged, giving s0(I)=(-1)^sum I. Literal Fock annihilation on all510 subsets for one through eight modes verifies this; the earlier formula incorporating −D(D−1)/2 fails255 subsets. The two-hole example c0c1|11>=−|00> is decisive. Retaining b_D as a separate optional unit-modulus block phase is valid. Every operator claimed here preserves D, so b_D cancels in the intertwining relation; that explains why the earlier conserving-operator tests could not detect the prose error. No off-D operator identity follows.
+
+## Domain, basis and operator proof
+
+On the black-to-white orientation, divE=epsilon(deg−3) exactly. Degree six makes it integer even in the enlarged spin-half carrier. No-double leaves three distinct charge states, so Gauss determines the matter state uniquely from electric bits; without it the zero-charge vacuum/double degeneracy invalidates the dimension argument. The displayed phase is nonzero on every source basis element, establishing onto isometry on the entire low domain, without a census. Closed torus neutrality implies D even and supplies the required parity consistency.
+
+Native occupation is1−Q². Particle-hole conjugation gives c_i†c_j=−h_j†h_i for distinct sites. In site-major two-species ordering, an allowed source-to-empty-target bilinear has the same intervening-occupied-site sign as one-hole CAR; the unused endpoint species slots are empty. Both occupied endpoints either vanish by Pauli exclusion or are killed by no-double projection. The charge-preserving electric increment chooses L− for a positive black-to-white move and L+ for a negative one. The reverse terms are adjoints. This establishes both allowed amplitudes and forbidden support, using the earlier full native W theorem rather than assuming unsigned hopping.
+
+Independent finite controls check400 allowed native hop columns and2096 gated ring columns on22 different-order actual L4 configurations spanning D=0,2,4,...,16,64. All agree exactly; removing the particle-hole minus fails every hop column. These controls do not enumerate the whole L4 Hilbert space. Their role is to challenge phase/order conventions in the general proof.
+
+For rings the alternating ladder support matches the gate, the source W removes the native cycle dressing, and unchanged Q leaves s0 and b_D unchanged. Ungated cycles are correctly excluded. The local gauge commutator is independently consistent: [G_v,f_(v,s)]=s f_(v,s), [G_i,L+]=L+, [G_j,L+]=−L+. Thus the charge weights cancel in each displayed bilinear, and P_nd commutes with every G. Projected f operators are explicitly not claimed to obey full CAR. Since each G has integer spectrum here,2pi periodicity is valid.
+
+## Source/model boundary
+
+The signed divergence charge is distinct from the old Noether charge |V|/2−D, and total signed Q vanishes on the torus. A constrained U1 presentation does not add physical link degrees of freedom or replace the older two-role model. Relaxed fixed-cycle constraints, low-charge gates, graph placement, Hamiltonian interpretation and coefficients remain supplied. The unitary is not a local circuit or a Record formation law. No deconfinement, QED, photon or axiomatic closure is established. Primary-literature comparison is separately recorded in ../native-low-charge-u1-prior-art/COMPARISON.md.
