+# Source and primary-literature comparison: low-charge native U1 candidate
+
+This is a bounded source/premise comparison, not a novelty or theorem verdict. The proposed target was supplied by root before this review. At the initial read the candidate directory contained its preregistration, complete check.py and RESULT.json but no written proof. Its later frozen proof requires a separate cold review. No author helper was rerun here.
+
+## Exact difference from the current supplied U1-link note
+
+The current main-worktree note THE_FERMIONS_U1_COUPLED_TO_QUANTUM_LINKS_GAUSS_LAW_AS_A_SUPPORT_CONDITION_AMONG_RECORDS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-03.md was read completely, including its correction boundary. It explicitly adds a designed second two-state role per coarse edge, independent of the BK fermion-edge role. It supplies a Hamiltonian, spin-half electric raising operator, Gauss kernel and finite geometries. The coupling pairs the existing encoded hopping and current partner with X/Y of the additional link. Its corrected one-corner projection identity is not global compatibility or a nearest-neighbor Record formation law. Its electric E² is constant and its off-diagonal observables lack a fixed-record readout.
+
+PR8038's current source was read completely at head86e03ef9a8eaafb9106304bf54cc0a991c758001. It instead maps the whole original edge space into a redundant CAR–Z2 tensor space with all-positive Gauss constraints, explicit basis phases and no new physical sites. It relaxes the old fixed-cycle state restriction. Its low-charge corollary supplies |deg(v)−3|≤1 on a six-valent bipartite graph. A new U1 representation built from that corollary would be an additional exact coordinate description of this supplied restricted space, not the old independently coupled model and not an axiom-derived choice of that restriction or Hamiltonian.
+
+The traded premises are concrete: fewer independent physical roles, but a low-charge domain, relaxed cycle constraints, bipartite orientation, redundant matter coordinates, exclusion of double occupancy and phase-correct projected operator identification. The larger redundant tensor product must not be counted as new accessible native degrees of freedom. No local physical circuit follows from a Hilbert-space unitary.
+
+## Independent algebraic checks and interpretation
+
+Write x_e=(1−Z_e)/2 and d_v=sum incident x_e. Orient each link from the even sublattice to the odd sublattice, and put E_e=x_e−1/2 on that orientation. Then div E_v=epsilon_v(d_v−3)=Q_v. On a coordinate-positive orientation, the equivalent field is E_(v,a)=epsilon_v(x_(v,a)−1/2); omitting epsilon there gives the wrong divergence. Degree six is load-bearing: at boundaries the offset is z_v/2, not automatically3. Periodic even extents preserve the bipartition; odd periodic extents do not.
+
+On d=2,3,4, B=(-1)^d equals+1,−1,+1. Consequently the native occupation n_f=(1−B)/2 equals1−Q². The old conserved Noether charge is sum(n_f−1/2)=|V|/2−sum Q². It is NOT the signed divergence charge sum Q, which vanishes identically on a closed oriented graph. The new plus/minus defect counts can be conserved under the projected hopping without identifying signed Q with the old Noether generator.
+
+In an ambient two-mode CAR Fock space per vertex, impose n_+ n_−=0. Then the allowed local labels are vacuum,+,−, and n_+−n_− has three distinct eigenvalues0,+1,−1. A given electric configuration with |Q|≤1 fixes the matter label uniquely. Thus the basis map |x> to |label(Q(x))> tensor |x> is isometric and onto the constrained Gauss basis. This proves the diagonal/basis part only; it does not establish native hopping phases. Removing no-double occupancy makes charge zero degenerate between vacuum and the two-particle state, immediately destroying the claimed uniqueness. Also, projected creation operators on the three-state carrier do not themselves satisfy unconstrained two-mode CAR; CAR belong to the ambient four-state space, and physical bilinears must be projected.
+
+The candidate's site-major species ordering, particle-hole minus sign, native ordered-star phases and electric ladder direction are therefore mathematical obligations, not notation. The author's global exchange witness has a six-hop phase−1, so replacing all signs by nonnegative hopping is not licensed. The proposed charge/flavor encoding can preserve this fermionic information; Gauss's law alone cannot.
+
+## Checked primary prior art and applicability
+
+Chandrasekharan and Wiese, Quantum Link Models, hep-lat/9609042v2, section3 equations3.5–3.17, explicitly construct U(1) link operators from spin raising/lowering operators and electric generators from spin-z divergences, including the two-dimensional link representation. This is the directly applicable standard algebraic precedent for a spin-half U1 quantum link. It does not prove the native embedding, supplied domain, fermionic phases, or a continuum phase. Their own discussion separates this finite link construction from continuum/dimensional-reduction arguments. Primary PDF: https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-lat/9609042.
+
+Zohar and Cirac, Eliminating fermionic matter fields in lattice gauge theories,1805.05347, sectionsII–IV, equations7–10 and the normal-Z2/representation qualification around sectionIII, supplies the relevant precedent that gauge constraints can transfer fermionic statistics into gauge variables. Its displayed U1 example uses a unitary link operator and [E,U]=U; its method requires an appropriate parity operator, not merely the name U1. The spin-half ladder is nonunitary, so I do not import the paper's whole theorem verbatim. The anticommutation of electric parity with a spin-half ladder can be checked directly, but that alone is not a native dictionary proof. Primary PDF: https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.05347.
+
+Zohar and Cirac, Removing Staggered Fermionic Matter in U(N) and SU(N) Lattice Gauge Theories,1905.00652, sectionIII equations24–30 and37–58, is the closest premise comparison. It emphasizes unique determination of matter by charge; multiple charge-degenerate matter states obstruct direct removal. Finite matter spaces leave local electric constraints and projectors, and fermionic signs must survive in the transformed interactions. Its initial U1 gauge carrier is rotor-like; its matter example is staggered single-species, not this opposite-charge no-double three-state space. Thus the candidate resembles inverse constrained matter elimination, but its carrier and intertwiner still require their own proof. Primary PDF: https://arxiv.org/pdf/1905.00652.
+
+These papers establish substantial standard methodology. No claim of historical priority follows from this limited search or from a failure to find the exact native formula. The potentially distinctive result is the explicit phase-correct equivalence for the already specified native operators and low-charge support, if independently proved.
+
+## Scope remaining unchanged
+
+The fine physical sites remain edge midpoints 2v+e_a; two coarse-adjacent edge sites are not automatically nearest-neighbor physical sites. Integer Gauss identities, finite Hamiltonians and diagonal record observables do not supply complete history-conditioned local probabilities, event formation, permanent-record-compatible dynamics or a compiler. This U1 is neither automatically the earlier global Noether U1 nor QED. No photon, deconfinement, relativistic species, action selection, physical gauge redundancy or continuum dynamics is obtained just by changing coordinates.
